@@ -257,3 +257,7 @@ Guideline 5.1.2(i) / APPI §28. Every server function that sends photos, words o
 ## Sign in with Apple revocation on account deletion (2026-10-03)
 
 Apple's account-deletion rule (TN3194): `deleteMyAccount` calls `revokeAppleForUser` (`src/lib/apple-revoke.server.ts`) after the data is deleted and before the auth user is deleted. It posts the stored token to `https://appleid.apple.com/auth/revoke` with an ES256 `client_secret` signed by Web Crypto (`src/lib/apple-revoke.ts`; env `APPLE_TEAM_ID`, `APPLE_KEY_ID`, `APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY`, `APPLE_SERVICES_ID`). It never throws: no token / missing secrets / Apple errors are logged and the deletion continues. The token comes from `session.provider_refresh_token`, which supabase-js emits once right after an Apple OAuth sign-in; `apple-token-capture.ts` (installed at the top of `__root.tsx`) sends it to `saveAppleToken`, which stores it in `apple_tokens` (migration `20261003150000`, service role only). `/native-auth` waits up to 3 s for that upload before handing the session to iOS. Whether the Lovable OAuth broker forwards `provider_refresh_token` must be checked after deploy (README.ja.md); if it does not, revocation is skipped and logged.
+
+## Final confirmation before Stripe Checkout (特商法 12条の6, 2026-10-03)
+
+Settings → CatchWords Pro: the buy buttons no longer go straight to Stripe. They open `ProCheckoutConfirm`, which shows (from `getBillingStatus`: Stripe prices and `trialEligibleDays`, i.e. the trial this user would actually get) the service and quantity, price and later payments, trial end date and first charge, payment timing and method, start of service, auto-renewal, order period, how to cancel (Billing Portal via 「サブスクリプションを管理」), withdrawal/refunds, and links to terms / 特商法 / privacy, with the button 「規約に同意して購入する（定期購入）」. Rows come from `src/lib/checkout-terms.ts`. `createCheckoutSession` requires `confirmed: true` plus the shown amount, currency and trial days and refuses with `BILLING_TERMS_CHANGED` if they differ from what it would charge. The Stripe Checkout page gets `locale` and a `custom_text.submit` note (subscription, auto-renewal, how to cancel) in the user's language.
